Verbatim copies of GARM's runner-install templates, from
github.com/cloudbase/garm at 33ec0921418a470ca7e00dfb20ae111595da24e1 (the rev
packages/garm pins), internal/templates/userdata/:

  linux_wrapper.tmpl, windows_wrapper.tmpl
      the install-script wrappers GARM >= 0.2 puts in a pool's
      runner_install_template extra spec (util.MaybeAddWrapperToExtraSpecs);
  github_linux_userdata.tmpl, github_windows_userdata.tmpl
      the system templates `github_linux` / `github_windows` that GARM seeds
      into its database and renders at "$METADATA_URL/install-script/".

The check t_garm_install_script_template_fixtures fails when any of them stops
being byte-identical to the packaged GARM source (up to a final newline,
which the end-of-file-fixer hook adds to github_windows_userdata.tmpl), so a GARM bump has to refresh
them (and re-run the guard tests against the new text).
